":"4ba22aa1ec2dd606995574d93d70c6c8a3744859","Node name for S&R":"easy showAnything","ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"input_ue_unconnectable":{},"version":"7.8"}},"widgets_values":["Gritty realistic live-action, handheld documentary energy, shot on a long lens with shallow depth of field. The scene is a narrow service alley at night: wet concrete underfoot, brick wall on one side, a dented metal door, a single sodium lamp overhead throwing hard amber light and deep shadow, thin steam drifting from a vent. Every shot stays in close-up or medium close-up so faces read clearly; the fight always drives from screen-left toward screen-right, with the taller man in the dark jacket pushing the shorter man in the grey hoodie backward toward the metal door at frame right. That direction never reverses.\n\nScene overview: two men, mid-twenties to thirties, already deep into a brawl when the clip begins — no warm-up, no circling, only impact and recoil.\n\n[0.00s-2.00s] Shot 1: Tight close-up on the shorter man's face, sweat on his brow, jaw clenched, eyes locked off-screen to the left. He is already mid-motion, having thrown a hook that has landed; he does not wind up again. A fist snaps in from frame left and clips his cheekbone. His head whips to the right, spittle flying, one eye squeezing shut. The camera shakes hard on impact with a small amplitude, then settles. He staggers one step toward frame right, boots skidding on wet concrete, and catches himself on the brick wall with his left palm.\n\n[2.00s-4.00s] Shot 2: Medium close-up, camera pushing in slowly. Continuing from his stagger, he does not reset his stance; he pivots off the wall and drives his shoulder into the taller man's chest. The taller man's dark jacket bunches as he is shoved backward, feet sliding toward the metal door at frame right, one arm flailing up to grab a fistful of grey hoodie fabric. Both bodies twist together, elbows and forearms colliding, a forearm pressed across a throat. The camera arcs a few degrees to keep both faces in frame, staying close.\n\n[4.00s-6.00s] Shot 3: Close-up on the taller man's face, pressed near the brick, temple against the wall, breath ragged, teeth bared. Continuing the same screen-rightward push, the shorter man slams him into the metal door; the door rattles in its frame, a hinge screeching. The taller man's head bounces off the panel, his eyes losing focus, then snapping back with fury. He grins through a split lip and says in a low, cracked voice, <d>[Chinese] 就这点力气？</d> His lips move in sync with the words. The shorter man's forearm tightens across his collarbone; the taller man's hand claws upward, grabbing a wrist. Hold on that locked tension as the frame ends.\n\nCamera: handheld throughout with restrained breathing shake; small-amplitude push-ins, one short arc, no wide shots, no pull-backs that shrink the faces.\n\nAudio: narrow alley ambience, distant traffic hum, a dripping pipe, the low buzz of the sodium lamp. Physical sounds sharp and close: knuckle impact on cheekbone, boot soles scraping wet concrete, fabric tearing, a body thudding against a metal door, the door's hinge shrieking. Both men breathing hard through their noses, a wet cough, a low pained grunt. One line of dialogue delivered hoarse and mocking. No music until the final half-second, where a single low percussive hit lands on the last frame.\n\nNo text, subtitles, captions, logos or watermarks. No extra characters entering frame. No cross-dissolves, fades or wipes. No slow-motion."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"Gritty realistic live-action, handheld documentary energy, shot on a long lens with shallow depth of field. The scene is a narrow service alley at night: wet concrete underfoot, brick wall on one side, a dented metal door, a single sodium lamp overhead throwing hard amber light and deep shadow, thin steam drifting from a vent. Every shot stays in close-up or medium close-up so faces read clearly; the fight always drives from s